# gdmcp Fortune-5 readiness profile

This projection separates MCP protocol completeness from enterprise production readiness.

## Required contract

- MCP protocol: 2026-07-28
- Official SDK language projections: 10
- Protocol features: 64
- Repository Fortune-5 capabilities: 19
- Proof surfaces per capability: positive execution, negative refusal, receipt/replay
- Total capability obligations: 57
- Deployment/control groups: 15
- Ambient/direct actuation: forbidden

## Promotion law

A structural profile is not a production crown. Promotion requires executed SLO evidence, security controls, receipt replay, qualification suites, and an exact-subject verifier receipt. A red Andon signal, breached error budget, invalid lifecycle transition, failed security admission, replay failure, or open resilience circuit blocks risky change.

## Platform controls

Global networking; workload identity and mTLS; HSM/KMS encryption; full OTLP observability; supervised container and serverless runtimes; transactional and object data controls; replayable event fabric; signed/SBOM supply chain; policy governance; multi-region DR; protected edge delivery; immutable evidence ledger; executable qualification suites.

The generated `gdmcp/fortune5/verify_readiness.py` validates structural closure only. It does not certify a deployed environment.
